{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"The 3D tiled G gives a ~7% speedup on the Gram part. That's the biggest single win I've found so far. Combined with a full 3D-reshape approach, we can avoid 4D tensor operations throughout.\n\nLet me now think about a bigger optimization. The Gram matrix approach costs 2 matmuls of size `(BH, L, L) @ (BH, L, L)` = 2 * BH*L^3 FLOPs. But there's also the G = x@x^T computation.\n\nWait - another thought. We need `||p1@x||` and `||p_mix@x||`. But `p_mix = (1-beta)*p0 + beta*p1`. \n\n`||p_mix @ x||^2 = ||(1-beta)*p0@x + beta*p1@x||^2`\n`= (1-beta)^2*||p0@x||^2 + beta^2*||p1@x||^2 + 2*(1-beta)*beta * (p0@x)·(p1@x)`\n\nThe dot product `(p0@x)·(p1@x) = sum_c (p0@x_c) * (p1@x_c) = sum_c sum_j p0_j * x_{j,c} * sum_k p1_k * x_{k,c}`\n`= sum_j sum_k p0_j * p1_k * sum_c x_{j,c}*x_{k,c} = p0 @ G @ p1^T` (diagonal elements only)\n\nActually, more carefully, `(p0@x)·(p1@x)` per row = `(p0 @ G) * p1` summed over last dim... no that's not right.\n\n`(p0@x) @ (p1@x)^T = p0 @ x @ x^T @ p1^T = p0 @ G @ p1^T`\nAnd we want the diagonal (same row dot product): `(p0@x)[i] · (p1@x)[i]` for each i.\nThat's `sum_j sum_k p0[i,j] * G[j,k] * p1[i,k] = (p0 * (G @ p1^T)^T).sum(-1)`... hmm.\n\nActually: `(p0 @ G) * p1` gives elementwise product, sum over last dim gives `sum_j (p0G)[i,j] * p1[i,j]`. But we want `sum_j sum_k p0[i,j] * G[j,k] * p1[i,k]` which is the same as `sum_j p0[i,j] * (G@p1^T)[j,i]`... let me think again.\n\n`p0 @ G @ p1^T` is shape (L, L) per head. The i-th diagonal is `sum_j sum_k p0[i,j] * G[j,k] * p1[i,k]`.\nThis equals `sum_j p0[i,j] * (G @ p1^T)[j,i]` which is `(p0 * (p1 @ G))[i].sum()`... wait.\n\nActually: `(p1 @ G)[i,k] = sum_j p1[i,j] * G[j,k]`\nSo `sum_k p0[i,k] * (p1 @ G)[i,k] = sum_k p0[i,k] * sum_j p1[i,j] * G[j,k]` = the dot product we want.\n\nYes! `(p0 @ x) · (p1 @ x)` per row = `(p0 * (p1 @ G)).sum(dim=-1)`.\n\nSo if we compute `p0G = p0 @ G` and `p1G = p1 @ G`, we can get:\n- `||p0@x||^2 = (p0G * p0).sum(-1)` \n- `||p1@x||^2 = (p1G * p1).sum(-1)`\n- `(p0@x)·(p1@x) = (p0G * p1).sum(-1) = (p1G * p0).sum(-1)`\n\nAnd then `||p_mix@x||^2 = (1-beta)^2 * (p0G*p0).sum(-1) + beta^2 * (p1G*p1).sum(-1) + 2*(1-beta)*beta * (p0G*p1).sum(-1)`\n\nThis uses the same 2 G-matmuls (p0@G and p1@G) but replaces the p_mix@G matmul with cheaper elementwise operations. Let me test this:\n<br>\n\nGood, 3D tiled G gives ~7% speedup on Gram. Now let me test a bigger idea: replacing `p_mix@G` matmul with elementwise combination of `p0@G` and `p1@G` results:\n</think>\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cd /workspace && python3 -c \\\"\nimport torch, time, math\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\nalpha, beta = 1.05, 7.5\nBH = B*H\n\nG = torch.randn(B, L, L)\nG = G @ G.transpose(-1,-2)  # make symmetric PSD\nG_tiled = G.expand(BH, L, L).contiguous()\n\np0 = torch.randn(B, H, L, L).softmax(dim=-1)\np1 = torch.randn(B, H, L, L).softmax(dim=-1)\np_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\n\np0_3d = p0.reshape(BH, L, L)\np1_3d = p1.reshape(BH, L, L)\np_mix_3d = p_mix.reshape(BH, L, L)\n\n# Current approach: p1@G + p_mix@G\nfor _ in range(3):\n    p1G = p1_3d @ G_tiled\n    norm1_sq = (p1G * p1_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    pmG = p_mix_3d @ G_tiled\n    normm_sq = (pmG * p_mix_3d).sum(dim=-1)\nt0 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(11):\n    p1G = p1_3d @ G_tiled\n    norm1_sq = (p1G * p1_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    pmG = p_mix_3d @ G_tiled\n    normm_sq = (pmG * p_mix_3d).sum(dim=-1)\nt1 = time.process_time_ns()\nprint(f'p1@G + p_mix@G: {(t1-t0)/11/1e6:.2f} ms')\n\n# Alternative: p0@G + p1@G, derive p_mix norm via combination\n# ||m||\"'^2 = (1-b)''^2*||u0||''^2 + b''^2*||u1||''^2 + 2*(1-b)*b * u0·u1\nfor _ in range(3):\n    p0G = p0_3d @ G_tiled\n    p1G = p1_3d @ G_tiled\n    norm0_sq = (p0G * p0_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    norm1_sq = (p1G * p1_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    dot = (p0G * p1_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    b0 = 1.0 - beta\n    normm_sq = b0*b0*norm0_sq + beta*beta*norm1_sq + 2.0*b0*beta*dot\nt0 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(11):\n    p0G = p0_3d @ G_tiled\n    p1G = p1_3d @ G_tiled\n    norm0_sq = (p0G * p0_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    norm1_sq = (p1G * p1_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    dot = (p0G * p1_3d).sum(dim=-1)\n    b0 = 1.0 - beta\n    normm_sq = b0*b0*norm0_sq + beta*beta*norm1_sq + 2.0*b0*beta*dot\nt1 = time.process_time_ns()\nprint(f'\"'p0@G + p1@G + combo: {(t1-t0)/11/1e6:.2f} ms')\n\n# Verify\nprint(f'norm1_sq diff: {(norm1_sq - (p1_3d @ G_tiled * p1_3d).sum(-1)).abs().max():.2e}')\n\npmG = p_mix_3d @ G_tiled\nnormm_ref = (pmG * p_mix_3d).sum(-1)\nprint(f'normm_sq diff: {(normm_sq - normm_ref).abs().max():.2e}')\nprint(f'normm_sq rel diff: {((normm_sq - normm_ref).abs() / normm_ref.abs().clamp(min=1e-30)).max():.2e}')\n\\\"\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
